research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-30198-40-support finite-dimensional norms, norm equivalence, and the coordinate model;
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log:30199:41-Lebl supports vector-valued limits, derivatives, integrals, and the mean-value
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-30200-42-inequality; Banakh and Oertel--Paat--Weismantel support the
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-30201-43-Levy--Steinitz/Steinitz statements, including the stronger arbitrary-norm
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-30202-44-dimension bound; Princeton gives the parallelogram-law obstruction for the
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log:30203:45-one-norm; Harvard gives the exact `xy/(x^2+y^2)` witness; Lebl/Trench support
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-30204-46-the uniform-convergence theorem and counterexample families; Alberta states
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log:30205:47-the uniform M/Dirichlet/Abel tests; and Trench plus the Dini convention source
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-30206-48:support Dini's theorem and its four hypothesis failures. The recorded
